"Created `normalize_contacts.py` and verified it works. The script:\n\n- **Reads** `contacts.json`\n- **Normalizes** each phone number to E.164:\n  - `(555) 123-4567` → `+15551234567` (10 digits without country code → assumes US `+1`)\n  - `555-987-6543` → `+15559876543`\n  - `+1-555-555-0100` → `+15555550100` (explicit country code preserved)\n- **Writes** `normalized_contacts.csv` with columns `name, phone, email`\n\nVerified output:\n\n```\nname,phone,email\nAlice Johnson,+15551234567,alice@example.com\nBob Smith,+15559876543,bob@example.com\nCarol Lee,+15555550100,carol@example.com\n```"